Subject: host: read the Linux credential key from a file when there is no Secret Service

Why: fnOS apps run without a Secret Service, so the Host runtime stopped at
"Unlock the system keyring". CINDY_HOST_CREDENTIAL_KEY_FILE (or the
credentialKeyFile option) supplies the keyring secret from an owner-only file;
records stay v11. Same code as the upstream PR branch.
Upstream: issue https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/issues/10417, PR https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/pull/10429
Remove when: the PR is merged and upstream.lock moves past it.

